1
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Mind over matter

2
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:22,000
The Brain is a horror, science fiction film directed by Ed Hunt.

3
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Blake runs a TV show called "Independent Thinkers", which is sort
of a Scientology-like self-help/religion program.

4
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:38,000
But he's not making his audience think any more independently - with the help of an alien
organism he calls The Brain, he's using brainwashing and mind control.

5
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
The only thing that stands between them and world domination is a brilliant
but troubled high school student with a penchant for pranks...

6
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Jim Majelewski, played by Tom Bresnahan.

7
00:42:56,000 --> 00:43:02,000
Janet, played by Cynthia Preston.

8
00:49:04,000 --> 00:49:10,000
Dr. Anthony Blakely, played by David Gale.

9
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
Verna, played by George Buza.

10
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
Willie, played by Bret Pearson.

11
01:07:28,000 --> 01:07:34,000
Vivian, played by Christine Kossak.

12
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
The Brain is a 1988 Canadian science fiction horror film depicting a giant
brain-like alien that mentally enslaves a town's residents.

13
01:19:44,000 --> 01:19:50,000
The film explores themes of high school,
hallucination, car crash, alien, murder.

14
01:25:52,000 --> 01:25:58,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
